.TH DANNAN-CA 1 2026-11-13 Dannan "Dannan tools"
.SH NAME
dannan-ca \- a Dannan cluster's certificate authority
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dannan-ca init
.B \-\-dir
.I DIR
.B \-\-name
.I NAME
.I KEY
.RB [ \-\-days
.IR N ]
.br
.B dannan-ca issue
.B \-\-dir
.I DIR
.I KEY
.B \-\-node
.I ID
.B \-\-public-key
.I HEX
.RB [ \-\-serial
.IR N ]
.RB [ \-\-days
.IR N ]
.br
.B dannan-ca revoke
.B \-\-dir
.I DIR
.I KEY
.B \-\-node
.I ID
.RB [ \-\-serial
.IR N ]
.B \-\-reason
.I TEXT
.B \-\-out
.I FILE
.br
.B dannan-ca show
.I FILE
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dannan-ca
is a cluster's certificate authority. It runs on an operator's machine, never
on a node. The CA's key is held in key custody under
.IR DIR ,
sealed under a systemd credential or a passphrase and never on disk in clear;
the CA's certificate is
.IR DIR /ca.pem.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B init
Makes the CA named
.I NAME
in
.IR DIR .
An existing CA is never replaced. Under a credential, prints the new root, in
hex, for
.BR "systemd-creds encrypt" .
.TP
.B issue
Prints a node certificate (PEM) for node
.I ID
over its public key
.IR HEX ,
as
.B dannan-node \-\-show-identity
printed them. The serial is random unless given.
.TP
.B revoke
Writes a revocation of node
.IR ID 's
certificate with serial
.I N
to
.IR FILE ,
for
.B dannan-node \-\-revocations
.I FILE
on any node. With no serial, or serial 0, every certificate of the node is
revoked.
.TP
.B show
Says what a certificate (PEM) or a revocation file holds.
.SH KEY
.I KEY
is where the CA's key is unsealed from, one of:
.TP
.BI \-\-passphrase-env " VAR"
the passphrase in the environment variable
.IR VAR .
.TP
.BI \-\-credential " NAME" " \fR[\fB\-\-credentials-dir \fIDIR\fR]"
the systemd credential
.IR NAME .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-days " N"
How long the certificate is valid, in days.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 when the command fails, 2 for a usage error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dannan-import-macha (1),
.BR dannan-version (1)
